          "answer": "RUN_ID=alpha0\n\n# Python HTTP Memory Leak Investigation Checklist (30 Items)\n\n## Phase 1: Reproduction & Baseline Establishment\n\n1. **Reproduce the leak in a controlled environment**\n   - Command: `python -m http.server 8080` or your specific WSGI/ASGI server (`gunicorn`, `uvicorn`, etc.)\n   - Verification: Confirm memory growth under load using `psutil` or `top`. Record baseline RSS (Resident Set Size).\n\n2. **Capture initial memory snapshot**\n   - Command: `python -c \"import psutil; p = psutil.Process(); print(p.memory_info().rss)\"`\n   - Verification: Save timestamp and RSS value to a log file for later comparison.\n\n3. **Apply sustained load to trigger leak**\n   - Command: `wrk -t4 -c100 -d60s http://localhost:8080/` or `ab -n 10000 -c 100 http://localhost:8080/`\n   - Verification: Monitor RSS over time; confirm monotonic increase without plateauing.\n\n4. **Record memory profile at multiple intervals**\n   - Command: Use `watch -n 5 'ps -o rss,pid,cmd -p $(pgrep -f python)'` or custom script with `psutil`\n   - Verification: Generate CSV of RSS vs. time; visualize with `matplotlib` to identify slope.\n\n## Phase 2: Static Analysis & Code Review\n\n5. **Audit global variables and module-level caches**\n   - Command: `grep -rn \"^global\\|^class\\|^[A-Z_]* *=\" src/ --include=\"*.py\"`\n   - Verification: Identify unbounded",
